OL,3,GNEWSAHow to spot a psychopath at work -
OL,4,Afrom a man who worried he could be one
OL,5,
OL,6,FMost of us have had colleagues who can
OL,7,Fbe tricky to work with.
OL,9,FThey may act impulsively, be
OL,10,Fmanipulative, or even outright lie to
OL,11,Fadvance their careers - but how can you
OL,12,Ftell the difference between an
OL,13,Funpleasant co-worker and someone
OL,14,Fdisplaying psychopathic traits?
OL,16,FGeraint Anderson, a former London
OL,17,Fbanker-turned author, said he was
OL,18,Fassessed by a clinical psychologist who
OL,19,Ftold him he might have had "situational
OL,20,Fpsychopathy" to succeed in the
OL,21,Fcut-throat corporate world.
OL,23,APub: 03-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
